*begin rowtencavebottom2	
*export 10 11
*team "Caroline" notes 								
*team "Holly Bradley" compass clino tape 
*team "Mike Butcher" backcompass backclino
*instrument "beardy's Tandum" compass							;It is important to enter which instrument was used (serial no. etc) as if one instrument later turns out to have an error, survey can automatically correct all results with this instrument 
*instrument "Beardy's Tandum" clino
*instrument "Beardy's Tandum" backcompass
*instrument "Beardy's Tandum" backclino

*date 2015.06.14
;*calibrate declination +2.64
;*calibrate backcompass 180								;This option is currently noted out. This can be used if backcompass readings are taken as fore-sights		
;*calibrate backclino 0 -1								;As above point

*data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino backclino		;This line of code specifically tells survex what order the data is being entered in. We need to keep this the same for all our surveys if possible
10	11	3.07	195	018	3	-1	
11	12	1.93	254	076	10	-11
12	13	4.24	203.5	022	0.5	-2
13	14	2.02	282	103	0.35	-5	
14	15	5.77	286	106	08	-6
15	16	11.3	340	161	2	0	
16	17	12.85	011	191	4	-2	


*data passage station left right up down							;This line defines the paramenters and order of data entry for LRUD's, this does not normally need to change. Survex will plot the left and right at each data point HALF WAY BETWEEN the proceeding leg and the next, so they might not come out as you expect from your sketch. With experience people will learn how to correct for this when note sketching in the cave
10	0	0.5	3	1.6	
11	0	0.75	3	1.3	
12	0.77	0	2.5	1.3
13	0	0.9	1.8	2.5	
14	0.9	0	1.8	1.7	
15	0.5	1.5	1.8	1
16	0.2	2.5	2.0	1.6
17	0	1.10	2	1.5

*end rowtencavebottom2													;This MUST be the same name as entered in the first line of the survex file. A classic mistake is to forget to change this line, and the survey will not work